Create_AgentOwner_Unit_Concrete_Test
├── when the caller is not the owner it names
│   └── it should revert with NotOwner
├── when the signer is the zero address
│   └── it should revert with InvalidSigner
├── when the signer is the owners sentinel
│   └── it should revert with InvalidSigner
├── when the signer is AgentOwner itself
│   └── it should revert with InvalidSigner
├── when the signer is the owner
│   └── it should revert with InvalidSigner
├── given the derived Safe already belongs to an agent
│   └── it should revert with AgentExists
├── given someone deployed the derived Safe through the factory first
│   ├── it should not call the factory again
│   ├── it should make AgentOwner the Safe's transaction guard and module guard
│   ├── it should swap the signer in as the one owner
│   └── it should record the agent and emit AgentCreated
├── when the factory deploys at another address than the derived one
│   └── it should revert with DerivedAddressMismatch
└── when the owner creates an agent for a valid signer
    ├── it should deploy the Safe through the Safe proxy factory with the Safe L2 singleton and the owner and signer salt
    ├── it should set up the Safe with AgentOwner as its one owner, threshold one and the 4337 module as fallback handler
    ├── it should swap the signer in as the one owner
    ├── it should enable the 4337 module and AgentOwner as modules
    ├── it should make AgentOwner the Safe's transaction guard and module guard
    ├── it should record the agent with its owner and signer, not frozen and not removed
    ├── it should emit AgentCreated
    └── it should return the Safe
